  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of emergency WASH and protection services in DeZ and Idlib governorate</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Over a decade of conflict, coupled with unprecedented inflation, soaring prices of essential commodities and constant disruption of basic services, the population residing in the most conflict -affected regions of Syria, such as Deir Ez -Zor and Idleb is confronted with a multifaceted crisis. The most dire needs are identified in the water and sanitation sector, which exposes the population to acute health and protection risks. Against this backdrop, Oxfam proposes the provision of the emergency water &amp; sanitation services to the most crisis -affected communities of Deir Ez -Zor, while extending assistance to the most in -need locations of Idleb governorate. With the proposed 24 -month programme, Oxfam is planning to provide a minimum standard of water security to a total of 62,400 most vulnerable individuals (44,900 in Deir ez -Zor, 17,500 in Idleb) residing in the hard -to -reach areas with a lack of/limited humanitarian presence. In addition, Oxfam is proposing to support 200 at -risk individuals in Idleb governorate with protection assistance via cash for protection or/and referrals to specialist services to address immediate shocks related to the dire economic situation and lack of purchasing power.</narrative>
  </description>
